{"title":"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9dfe7c7a0b887097fa2227a230fc915ba2e5477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3eeefa367883375994fd2e1f575d088bce9d8b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/5/ca59e861f7103ff5a48adc6c4521ad936504c772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> are all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polynomial\" title=\"Polynomial\">polynomials</a> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7cd8a121a26324cfb87e8329bbd724c7792dcb4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(x^5) + xQ(x^5) + x^2 R(x^5) = (x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x +1) S(x),\\]\" width=\"451\" height=\"20\" />\nprove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4baf6d4b1cfa69b68b3204b5e2eba0c5755fe20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In general we will show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb48ab3c9d9054b4f5c325b8b8ed71fad63a0939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0, \\dotsc, P_{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are polynomials satisfying\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119dc61fef7435eb02f218bf293a895f6e40e5e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P_0(x^n) + x P_1(x^n) + \\dotsb + x^{m-1} P_{m-1}(x^n) = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} x^k S(x),\\]\" width=\"430\" height=\"50\" />\nthen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/a/3ca55f008017ce4ea6c74df3eb0398bcc4d128a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k(1) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />, for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce793d354da1cd9a3fb67a65d486037d37038ceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le k \\le m-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" />.  For the problem, we may set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84e75ddd39b9408f4d8e7fa62d2f6cdca00232de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904f27995d33e0d39f43ec959e7cb100516e9396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, and then note that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/962e5000c09e88b5ca898360c9ed8da40ad27120.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(1)= 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2e5691ba4f99b8214facf133f0e95fafa5db4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Indeed, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/1/d214a0e78e02cb849c967bffdd89a1e102c6142e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega_1, \\dotsc, \\omega_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"11\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Roots_of_unity\" title=\"Roots of unity\">roots of unity</a> other than 1.  Then for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff83105557fa452974107ed1f164b322e4fe8fd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/8936a78389a005e47dbd4148ea7010a0b3234038.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=0}^{m-1} \\omega_i^k P_k(\\omega_i^n) = \\sum_{k=0}^{m-1} \\omega_i^k P_k(1) = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\omega_i^k S(\\omega_i) = \\frac{\\omega_i^{n-1} - 1}{\\omega_i - 1} S(\\omega_i) = 0 ,\\]\" width=\"520\" height=\"50\" />\nfor all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd77e67d5e894bf1026f4cffd551f2856f52af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />.  This means that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e872b1716e55bea35303b2aa0c42770b1da5ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />th degree polynomial\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f553089fd3e8c49d4b45388c33aa8f6d3177f59e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=0}^{m-1} x^k P_k(1)\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"50\" />\nhas <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6f17346b47494dd7ad151b168c2c5026138817c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1 &gt; m-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"112\" height=\"12\" /> distinct roots.  Therefore all its coefficients must be zero, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5cc3f1407458d80f5a3af4487770f80309f90f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce793d354da1cd9a3fb67a65d486037d37038ceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le k \\le m-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" />, as desired.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/0/b808305fa1b7a7d31ab03db21da022eaf74fd706.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta, \\xi, \\rho$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> be three distinct primitive fifth <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Roots_of_unity\" title=\"Roots of unity\">roots of unity</a>.\nSetting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a01a4c87e15b593240bcebb734302a35c8c0179c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\zeta, \\xi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f561762a4aab179558a6dd2fb53fee5583e69ea6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} P(1) + \\zeta Q(1) + \\zeta^2 R(1) &amp;= \\frac{\\zeta^5-1}{\\zeta-1} S(\\zeta) = 0, \\\\ P(1) + \\xi Q(1) + \\xi^2 R(1) &amp;= \\frac{\\xi^5-1}{\\xi-1} S(\\xi) = 0 . \\end{align*}\" width=\"331\" height=\"91\" />\nThese equations imply that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e04211a4161629fe75b41fbc0396188130769219.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\zeta Q(1) + \\zeta^2 R(1) = \\xi Q(1) + \\xi^2 R(1),\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"19\" />\nor\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/65986e33a3ff5fedb8185aa6ec66d0212301b485.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q(1) = - ( \\zeta + \\xi)R(1).\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" />\nBut by symmetry,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e605b3d50717e2b95e7aa045c09054b70ed8db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Q(1) = - (\\zeta + \\rho)R(1) .\\]\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be171487dcf6d911afab1e1dc75896de5a7c5c42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\xi \\neq \\rho$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb47d4b1f783341c529cc9edb4c258125155d395.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(1) = R(1) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />.  Then, as noted above,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fac5e9f973f34ac1cb772c4728fba42b82843b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(1) = P(1) + \\zeta Q(1) + \\zeta^2 R(1) = 0,\\]\" width=\"281\" height=\"19\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2e5691ba4f99b8214facf133f0e95fafa5db4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />, as desired.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f48da5eeebddefcfe5963009c8a9d5f3c81aff9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z, z^2, z^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> be three of the 5th roots of unity not equal to one that satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c5e7dd1564fb06e0e957904ddc73eb2ee90729e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + z + z^2 + z^3 + z^4 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"190\" height=\"16\" /> as a result. Plugging them into the equation gives the linear system of equations in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/5/fc562fc504ab3a6769aece7838124ac1843bf3aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A(1), B(1), C(1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a9759ebbecb6677166598d113b3fbfd060cb0351.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A(1) + zB(1) + z^2C(1) = 0\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/4/824e87be5afc4135fec5392eeeb1a70636b4338d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A(1) + z^2B(1) + z^4C(1) = 0\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/322291217e4e3195f68dcfe9bc2675a2d51f492a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A(1) + z^3B(1) + z^6C(1) = 0\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Direct observation gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c172bfd9bd4a6b69e3925afca4b9bff323a3dcb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A(1), B(1), C(1)) = (0,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"223\" height=\"18\" /> as a solution, and there are no others because the system of equations is linear. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/e/b4e3cabf33f86e4302d78c3774f8e6974810d02d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(1) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2e5691ba4f99b8214facf133f0e95fafa5db4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/133abca2101afa88a51f60a6747c47e699a858e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" />, as desired. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><i>Note: We can generalize this approach to prove the claim in Solution 1 in an equally fast, concise, and readily understandable fashion.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO\" title=\"1976 USAMO\">1976 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1976\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1976 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?p=523481#523481\">Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017172314\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 316/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1237/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9946/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.801      1 -total\n 56.72%    6.694      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 40.75%    4.809      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6107:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017172314 and revision id 71654. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}